import{_ as o,o as t,c,a2 as d}from"./chunks/framework.BM5YPQmL.js";const v=JSON.parse('{"title":"Block drivers","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"l1/driver-block.md","filePath":"l1/driver-block.md"}'),a={name:"l1/driver-block.md"};function r(i,e,s,l,n,h){return t(),c("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[d('<h1 id="block-drivers" tabindex="-1">Block drivers <a class="header-anchor" href="#block-drivers" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Block drivers&quot;">​</a></h1><p>How a storage device family joins the block service so the whole system (VFS, partitions, fs utilities, the disk-tool wizard) sees it.</p><h2 id="the-model-3-0-0" tabindex="-1">The model (3.0.0) <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-model-3-0-0" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;The model (3.0.0)&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Drivers live in <code>ocos/drivers/storage/</code> - one file pair per family (<code>drv_storage_ahci.{c,h}</code>, <code>drv_storage_nvme.*</code>, <code>drv_storage_ata*</code>, <code>drv_storage_virtio_blk.*</code>, <code>drv_storage_scsi*</code>, <code>drv_storage_sdhci.*</code>).</li><li>Identity is declared with <code>OC_DRIVER_DECL(&quot;block&quot;, &quot;ahci&quot;, &amp;ops, &quot;SATA AHCI&quot;)</code> - a const descriptor the boot collector walks. No global registry edits, no init-call chains by hand.</li><li>The driver mutates the block service&#39;s device table only from inside its own probe/detach path through the driver-internal API (<code>drv_storage_api.h</code>: <code>driver_block_add_device</code> / <code>remove_device</code>; <code>BLK_MAX_DEVICES</code> slots, 512-byte sectors, 32-char names). The register-class entries were removed in v2.0.0 - this header is kernel-internal, NOT an L1 surface.</li><li>The hardware profile knobs (<code>CONFIG_NVME</code> / <code>CONFIG_AHCI</code> / <code>CONFIG_VIRTIO_BLK</code>, <code>make defconfig</code> / <code>menuconfig</code>) compile individual families out; the init calls are macro-stubbed by <code>core/generated/config_gen.h</code>.</li></ul><h2 id="the-service-side" tabindex="-1">The service side <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-service-side" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;The service side&quot;">​</a></h2><p><code>ocos/services/block/</code> fronts the L1SVC category 2 surface: device listing (<code>lsblk</code>), partition tables (<code>parted</code>), mkfs (FAT32 / exFAT / ext4), <code>fsck</code>, <code>sync</code>, the A/B disk tools (<code>abdisk</code>, <code>install</code>, <code>grub-install</code>, <code>abcfg</code>), the disk stats, and the test family (<code>ahci_test</code> .. <code>fs_mount_test</code>). The cache gate (64 slots) sits between the service and the drivers.</p><h2 id="what-a-new-family-looks-like" tabindex="-1">What a new family looks like <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-a-new-family-looks-like" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;What a new family looks like&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><code>ocos/drivers/storage/drv_storage_&lt;fam&gt;.{c,h}</code> - probe the bus, read the capacity, <code>driver_block_add_device()</code> per found disk.</li><li>One <code>OC_DRIVER_DECL(&quot;block&quot;, &quot;&lt;fam&gt;&quot;, &amp;ops, &quot;description&quot;)</code> line at the bottom.</li><li>A status op (if the family deserves one) in the service, an op number APPENDED to <code>svc_sysapi_l1svc.h</code> (append-only!), the mirror regenerated (<code>tools/gen_l1svc_ops.py</code>).</li><li>The app side: a thin wrapper folder or a row in a mega-app&#39;s classic table (<code>disk-tool</code>&#39;s <code>g_ops[]</code> is the pattern).</li></ol><h2 id="the-consumer-contract" tabindex="-1">The consumer contract <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-consumer-contract" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;The consumer contract&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Apps never touch drivers: they call the service (<code>disk-tool lsblk</code> -&gt; <code>sys_l1svc(BLOCK, LSBLK, ...)</code>). Device names are the stable contract (<code>hd0</code>, <code>hd0p1</code>, ...); the wizards show <code>lsblk</code> and ask for names by that spelling.</p>',10)])])}const p=o(a,[["render",r]]);export{v as __pageData,p as default};
